============================================================
  HUMAN FINDINGS GATE
============================================================

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  SUMMARY
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  The bug and fix are both confirmed. When KV cache pressure causes preemptions, BLIS was double-counting output tokens due to a ProgressIndex reset, inflating total_output_tokens by 9.1% (114,630 vs correct 105,082 for 200 requests with 265 preemptions). The fix—subtracting previously-counted tokens at preemption time—eliminates the inflation entirely, and all three KV cache configurations now report identical total_output_tokens=105,082.

  * h-main CONFIRMED: Pre-fix with tight KV cache (600 blocks, 265 preemptions) reported total_output_tokens=114,630 — a 9,548 token inflation (+9.1%). Post-fix, the same configuration reports 105,082, matching the no-preemption baseline exactly.
  * h-control-negative CONFIRMED: With large KV cache (60,000 blocks, 0 preemptions), total_output_tokens=105,082 both before and after the fix. The fix code path is never reached, confirming it is inert when no preemptions occur.
  * Root cause verified: ProgressIndex reset to 0 in sim/batch_formation.go:preemptForTokens caused TotalOutputTokens to be re-counted from scratch in sim/simulator.go:647. The fix stores OutputTokensGenerated before reset and subtracts it in the preemption handler.
  * A new regression test (TestSimulator_PreemptionDoesNotInflateTotalOutputTokens) passes with 11 preemptions observed, and all existing sim/... tests continue to pass.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

