────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  SUMMARY
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Iteration 1 fully resolved the reported bug: a preemption-driven double-counting error was inflating total_output_tokens by up to 9.1% (9,548 tokens on 265 preemptions). The fix—subtracting already-counted output tokens at preemption time and resetting TTFT/ITL state—produces identical token counts (105,082) across all KV cache sizes, and a new regression test passes.

  * Bug confirmed and fixed: pre-fix, 265 preemptions inflated total_output_tokens from 105,082 to 114,630 (+9.1%); post-fix, all three KV cache sizes (600, 6,000, 60,000 blocks) produce exactly 105,082.
  * Root cause was ProgressIndex reset to 0 in batch_formation.go:232 causing decode-loop increments in simulator.go:647 to re-count tokens from restarted requests; fix stores OutputTokensGenerated before the reset and subtracts it in the preemption handler.
